VERDICT: PROCEED WITH CHANGES -- The core sketch implements the rulings; correct the interim contract and wide-write diagnostic, and close the detector’s direction/width announcement gaps.

Q1 — The word census and zero invariant hold; the exception claim needs qualification, and the producer requires natural alignment.

**(a)** I enumerated the header’s register definitions against the switch, rather than treating every numeric `VME2_*` macro as a register. The results are:

- CASED, **10**: `00,2c,4c,50,54,60,6c,80,84,88`.
- Population 2, **26**: `04,08,0c,10,14,18,1c,20,24,28,30,34,38,3c,40,44,48,58,5c,64,68,70,74,78,7c,8c`.
- Population 1, **988 word starts**: enumerating `range(0x90,0x1000,4)` produced 28 starts in the first `0x100` block and 64 in each remaining block.

Sources: [mvme88k_vme.h:46](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/include/thirdparty/mvme88k_vme.h:46), [dev_vme.c:68](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:68).

**(b)** Initialization zeroes the array. Subsequent writers touch only word indices `{20,21,24,34}`: T1CMP, T1COUNT—including its read increment—TCTL and VBR. DEVINIT also seeds VBR. None is a population-2 index. Thus the population-2 zero invariant holds throughout the modeled device lifetime. Sources: [dev_vme.c:87](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:87), [dev_vme.c:101](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:101), [dev_vme.c:134](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:134), [dev_vme.c:158](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:158).

**(c)** An ordinary guest load/store reaching this callback uses `CACHE_DATA`, without `NO_EXCEPTIONS`; callback failure requests a data-access exception and returns failure. It does not silently complete the load. However:

- `NO_EXCEPTIONS` suppresses exception delivery. Because VME uses `DM_DEFAULT`, that path actually skips its callback and can return success with a zero-filled read buffer. Debugger memory inspection therefore cannot substitute for executing guest loads.
- Instruction fetch selects **instruction-access**, rather than data-access.
- An already-set PSR.SFRZ converts the requested nontrap exception into ERROR. Expected PC `0x18` requires VBR zero and an appropriate initial PSR.

Sources: [cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:60](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:60), [memory_rw.c:485](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:485), [memory_rw.c:583](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:583), [dev_vme.c:164](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:164), [cpu_m88k.c:811](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k.c:811), [cpu_m88k.c:863](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k.c:863).

**(d)** Enumerating the actual producer domain gives, per direction:

| Callback `len` | Reachable offsets | Count | CASED bases | Population-2 bases | Starts ≥ `0x90` |
|---:|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 1 | `0,1,…,fff` | 4096 | 10 | 26 | 3952 |
| 2 | `0,2,…,ffe` | 2048 | 10 | 26 | 1976 |
| 4 | `0,4,…,ffc` | 1024 | 10 | 26 | 988 |
| 8 | `0,8,…,ff8` | 512 | 5 | 13 | 494 |

Total: **7680 `(offset,len)` pairs**. The remaining pairs are interiors of cased words, **40**, and population-2 words, **104**.

Misaligned halfwords/words never reach VME. Neither does `ld.d` at an offset that is 4 mod 8. An aligned doubleword reaches **one eight-byte callback**, not two word callbacks. No enumerated pair crosses the memory dispatcher’s 1 KiB split boundary or this device’s end. Sources: [cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:167](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:167), [cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:189](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:189), [cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:234](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:234), [memory_rw.c:186](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:186).

Q2 — The executable paths are sound for the stated scope; the default-arm explanation is inaccurate.

Walking the original function with packet §5 applied:

- Writes decode `idata`; reads preload one array word. Dispatch bounds keep that index within the array. Sources: [dev_vme.c:60](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:60), [memory_rw.c:480](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:480).
- `0`, GCSRCTL, TCR, IRQEN, IRQL3 and IRQL4 retain their existing behavior. T1CMP, TCTL and VBR store only on writes. T1COUNT reads return the **pre-increment** value, then increment storage by 100. Source: [dev_vme.c:70](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:70).
- The proposed population-2 arm stores no register data, announces through a bounded, unique bit, then reaches the normal success tail. Its read diagnostic does not consume `idata` (packet §5).
- Default failure correctly skips successful serialization and `return 1`. The memory layer has already zeroed the caller’s read buffer, so “writes no data back” should mean **no successful result or destination-register update**, not “the buffer is untouched.” Sources: [dev_vme.c:146](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:146), [memory_rw.c:485](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/memory_rw.c:485), [cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:189](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:189).

Replace “no register is defined here” in packet §5: default also receives interior offsets of **defined** registers. State that these are unsupported offsets, including the disclosed interim lane limitations.

Q3 — Omit `odata = 0` here; no current population-2 word-start read can preload nonzero storage.

The writer enumeration in Q1 proves the invariant. Even a wide store in a cased arm assigns only its indexed `uint32_t`; buffer serialization does not write adjacent device words. Sources: [dev_vme.c:85](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/devices/dev_vme.c:85), [memory.c:89](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/core/memory.c:89).

Your lean is sound: an explicit zero would hide a future population-2 backing-store edit from the proposed readback oracle. Document the zero-storage invariant next to the decline arm. The omission preserves useful regression sensitivity; it does not by itself prove that every possible side effect is absent.

Q4 — Keep exact labels as the interim implementation, explicitly widen the disclosure, and correct the halfword example.

A **byte at `0x29`** reaches VME default. A **halfword at `0x29`** fails alignment before reaching VME; use **`0x2a`** for that device-level test. Source: [cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:167](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_m88k_instr_loadstore.c:167).

Enumeration finds 78 byte starts and 26 aligned halfword starts inside population-2 words: **104 pairs**. Name these explicitly in the contract and widened `vmewidthlanes` scope, with their own interim regression pin.

Containing-word decoding would instead make those pairs decline and share their containing register’s latch. Restrict such decoding to population 2 if chosen; masking the whole switch would also change cased-register behavior. That is a larger lane-policy change than this sketch needs.

Neither choice changes the cited word-width guest sites. Those sites and field types are confirmed by [guest vme.c:452](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/dev/vme.c:452), [guest vme.c:576](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/dev/vme.c:576), and [guest vme.h:140](C:/DocumentNoSnc/cc/GXEMUL/_guest-src-openbsd22/sys/arch/mvme88k/dev/vme.h:140). The detector must pin whichever interior policy is selected.

